/// Checks play in server.network over real TCP on 127.0.0.1, in the flat world: what a player
/// is sent as they join, their chunks a batch at a time, their view following them, the
/// teleport they're to accept before they move, what other players see as they come and go, and
/// chat: messages to everyone, what's refused, spam, commands, which are all unknown so far, and
/// signed chat, with chat sessions whose keys a test key signs where Mojang's would, and the
/// console's commands, with `stop` and the console's request to stop. Each server
/// records what it's handed, and a server made the same way replays it at the end, sending and
/// logging the same (D21).
///
/// Every packet a client is sent goes to `build/packets/play.bin` too, for vanilla's own codecs
/// to read: a test client made from Calcite's code agrees with Calcite on every mistake, and
/// vanilla's doesn't (D145).
module test.play

